all_output.txt
# `result` is the default nix build link; the run skill also asks for
# result-h2ded and result-demodata, and a release build drops result-<target>.
result
result-*
.flatpak-builder/
audit.md
# engine/build/ is the default; the second renderer configuration needs its own
# CMake cache, so the whole family is ignored (scripts/wasm-build.sh takes the
# build directory as its second argument).
engine/build*/
# Assembled by scripts/wasm-assemble-artifact.sh -- engine/build/bin output
# copied over web/, i.e. entirely derived and multi-MB.
/dist/
*.o
*.d

# The beads (bd) issue tracker is retired; nothing under .beads/ is tracked any
# more, including the issues.jsonl export that used to be.  The rules stay so a
# leftover local install -- the Dolt database alone runs to ~100 MB -- cannot
# walk back into the history it was just taken out of.
.beads/
.bv/

# RenderDoc captures and the artifacts of picking one apart.  A .rdc is tens
# to hundreds of MB (the three sitting in this tree when the rule was widened
# came to 166 MB), and `renderdoccmd convert -c zip.xml` spits out an equally
# disposable .xml beside it.  They are debugging scratch for one bug -- the
# findings belong in the bead, the capture does not belong in history, where
# it cannot be taken back out.  Root-anchored so a mod or tool directory that
# legitimately ships an .xml is unaffected.
/*.rdc
/*.xml
# A part-downloaded capture is still a capture, and the frame images
# extracted out of one are the same disposable scratch.
/*.crdownload
/capture*_frame*
/torch_glow_ab*

# Dolt working files, left behind by the retired beads tracker.
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
/image4.png

# The Hexen II demo tarball is fetched, not committed: 13 MB of binary, and we
# have no right to redistribute it -- the only licence shipped with it is
# Activision's retail EULA, which forbids distributing copies (uhexen2-3vmk).
# Users fetch it themselves via scripts/get_demo.sh / .cmd.  See
# assets/demo/README.md for the source URL, sha256 and the full reasoning.
/assets/demo/hexen2demo_nov1997-linux-i586.tgz

# tools/*.py are runnable scripts, but importing them (as the qcdis.py
# self-checks do) leaves a bytecode cache behind.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
